# Routes 216 and 217 and Acuity Lakefront (the original's ROAD_SNOW role): the snowbound roads north of Mt. Coronet,
# drifts up to the knee, a blizzard in the face and the lake waiting at the end. A determined G-minor march into the
# wind: the violin strides out in dotted steps over a piano tramping in eighths and a bass that never stops walking,
# the snare like boots in the snow and the shaker hissing like the gusts; the horn leans in beside it for a braver
# E-flat stretch, icy glockenspiel flurries end each phrase, and four bars of the wind alone push on to the dominant.
# By night a flute and a clarinet over a harp and a pad. Original composition for this game.
title Route 216
tempo 120
meter 4/4
reverb 0.34
nighttempo 0.93

